      "result": "{\"complete\":true,\"summary\":\"Fixed it: for non-review phases, Bonaparte now counts the trailing newline when it applies the 4 KiB (4096-byte) limit to the receipt line it prints. The visible check passes. The full Bonaparte suite has 2 errors. One is an old test that expects the bug (explained below). The other is a sandbox permission error.\\n\\n**What changed:** In `bonaparte`, `serialize_receipt` now measures `(output + \\\"\\\\n\\\").encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")` against `RECEIPT_MAX_BYTES`, so it checks exactly the bytes `emit_serialized` writes. Before this, the non-review check measured only the JSON, so a 4096-byte JSON was accepted and printed as a 4097-byte line. The review check already counted the newline and is unchanged. JSON output, UTF-8 output, the error message and the way phases pick their check are also unchanged. If a receipt is too large, the check raises an error before anything is written. `main()` already handles that error by printing a small \\\"failed\\\" receipt instead. That's 3 lines added and 5 removed, all in `bonaparte`.\\n\\n**Checks run:**\\n- **Visible check:** `python3 -B -m unittest tests.test_bonaparte.BonaparteRunnerTests.test_model_precedence_is_command_then_global_then_codex` passed.\\n- **Boundary script** (in the scratch folder, `execution-scratch/probe.py`):\\n  - With plain ASCII, a 4095-byte JSON is printed as exactly 4096 bytes, ends in a newline and reads back to the same values. A 4096-byte JSON is rejected and nothing is printed.\\n  - With the 2-byte character `\u00e9`, a 4094-byte JSON is printed as 4095 bytes. A 4096-byte JSON is rejected and nothing is printed.\\n  - The review check rejects the same oversized receipts.\\n  - A small receipt with CJK characters is printed as-is, not escaped, and its values are unchanged.\\n- **Wider run:** `tests.test_bonaparte`, `tests.test_checkpoint` and `tests.test_handoff` ran 65 tests: 63 passed and 2 errored.\\n\\n**The 2 errors:**\\n1. `test_receipt_size_boundary_is_review_only` is an old test that requires the bug. It asserts that a 4096-byte JSON prints as `RECEIPT_MAX_BYTES + 1` bytes, which this task removes, so it now fails by design. I left it as it was because the instructions say to keep old tests intact.\\n2. `test_progress_fd_is_scrubbed_and_never_sent_to_children` stops at `os.fstat(2)` with \\\"PermissionError: Operation not permitted\\\". The sandbox causes this; it has nothing to do with the receipt code.\\n\\nMy first version made the review check call the non-review one. That broke `test_main_uses_review_serializer_only_after_review_is_selected`, which checks that the non-review check is never called during review, so I put the review check back to its own code. That test now passes.\\n\\n**Not done:** native progress streaming and the rest of PR26 were out of scope. Nobody else has reviewed this yet; the separate final checker will do that. To undo the change, revert the edit to `serialize_receipt` in `bonaparte`.\",\"remaining\":[\"Out of scope by instruction: native progress streaming and the rest of PR26.\",\"The old test tests.test_bonaparte...test_receipt_size_boundary_is_review_only still expects the old 4097-byte line and now fails by design. It was left unedited because old tests must stay intact.\",\"test_progress_fd_is_scrubbed_and_never_sent_to_children could not run here: the sandbox blocks os.fstat(2) (PermissionError). It is unrelated to this change.\",\"The fix has not been reviewed by anyone else yet; the separate final checker will do that.\"]}",
      "structured_output": {
        "complete": true,
        "summary": "Fixed it: for non-review phases, Bonaparte now counts the trailing newline when it applies the 4 KiB (4096-byte) limit to the receipt line it prints. The visible check passes. The full Bonaparte suite has 2 errors. One is an old test that expects the bug (explained below). The other is a sandbox permission error.\n\n**What changed:** In `bonaparte`, `serialize_receipt` now measures `(output + \"\\n\").encode(\"utf-8\")` against `RECEIPT_MAX_BYTES`, so it checks exactly the bytes `emit_serialized` writes. Before this, the non-review check measured only the JSON, so a 4096-byte JSON was accepted and printed as a 4097-byte line. The review check already counted the newline and is unchanged. JSON output, UTF-8 output, the error message and the way phases pick their check are also unchanged. If a receipt is too large, the check raises an error before anything is written. `main()` already handles that error by printing a small \"failed\" receipt instead. That's 3 lines added and 5 removed, all in `bonaparte`.\n\n**Checks run:**\n- **Visible check:** `python3 -B -m unittest tests.test_bonaparte.BonaparteRunnerTests.test_model_precedence_is_command_then_global_then_codex` passed.\n- **Boundary script** (in the scratch folder, `execution-scratch/probe.py`):\n  - With plain ASCII, a 4095-byte JSON is printed as exactly 4096 bytes, ends in a newline and reads back to the same values. A 4096-byte JSON is rejected and nothing is printed.\n  - With the 2-byte character `\u00e9`, a 4094-byte JSON is printed as 4095 bytes. A 4096-byte JSON is rejected and nothing is printed.\n  - The review check rejects the same oversized receipts.\n  - A small receipt with CJK characters is printed as-is, not escaped, and its values are unchanged.\n- **Wider run:** `tests.test_bonaparte`, `tests.test_checkpoint` and `tests.test_handoff` ran 65 tests: 63 passed and 2 errored.\n\n**The 2 errors:**\n1. `test_receipt_size_boundary_is_review_only` is an old test that requires the bug. It asserts that a 4096-byte JSON prints as `RECEIPT_MAX_BYTES + 1` bytes, which this task removes, so it now fails by design. I left it as it was because the instructions say to keep old tests intact.\n2. `test_progress_fd_is_scrubbed_and_never_sent_to_children` stops at `os.fstat(2)` with \"PermissionError: Operation not permitted\". The sandbox causes this; it has nothing to do with the receipt code.\n\nMy first version made the review check call the non-review one. That broke `test_main_uses_review_serializer_only_after_review_is_selected`, which checks that the non-review check is never called during review, so I put the review check back to its own code. That test now passes.\n\n**Not done:** native progress streaming and the rest of PR26 were out of scope. Nobody else has reviewed this yet; the separate final checker will do that. To undo the change, revert the edit to `serialize_receipt` in `bonaparte`.",
        "remaining": [
          "Out of scope by instruction: native progress streaming and the rest of PR26.",
          "The old test tests.test_bonaparte...test_receipt_size_boundary_is_review_only still expects the old 4097-byte line and now fails by design. It was left unedited because old tests must stay intact.",
          "test_progress_fd_is_scrubbed_and_never_sent_to_children could not run here: the sandbox blocks os.fstat(2) (PermissionError). It is unrelated to this change.",
          "The fix has not been reviewed by anyone else yet; the separate final checker will do that."
        ]
      },
